Sorting and Filter options for case listing page details 

  

  

  

  

  

  

Overview 

Details 

Assignee 

Description 

  

Value Statement: 

As a User, 

I want sort and filter options available in the Case listing page 

So that, I can check and prioritize the recovery processing activities. 

  

Process Overview 

Sorting and filtering options in the Cases page allow users to efficiently find and prioritize recovery claims. Filters and sorts are tailored to user roles and case data, enabling targeted access, prioritization, and improved workflow efficiency. 

Acceptance Criteria 

Filtering 

Workstream Filter 

Only managers see Workstream as a dropdown (Triage/Agency, Client/Title, Homeowner, Quality Check, Management/Payments). For other roles, Workstream is displayed as read-only, reflecting their assignment. 

Selecting a workstream as a manager lists all claims in that workstream; other personas see only claims assigned to them. 

  

Manager: 

  

  

Researcher: 

  

  

Assignment Status Filter 

All user personas can filter on Assignment Status, with dropdown options:  

All (Excluding Completed) – default, lists open/non-completed claims. 

Unassigned 

Assigned 

In Progress 

On Hold 

Completed 

  

  

Duration Filter 

All personas have this filter, based on when claims were added to UTW Recoveries:  

7 Days (default): Last 7 days 

1 Month: Last month 

3 Months: Last 3 months 

Custom: User can specify a custom range 

  

  

Client Filter 

All users can filter claims by client, selecting from a dropdown list of client names. This option is not needed as we imple 

  

  

Sorting 

Fields in the case listing table with sorting capability display up/down arrows in the column headers. 

Clicking a sortable column toggles sort order; sorting affects only the claims currently listed for the user. 

Sorting is enabled for:  

Base Amount: Sorts numerically (ascending/descending) 

Claim Balance: Sorts numerically (ascending/descending) 

Tax Agency: Sorts alphabetically (A–Z/Z–A) 

Next Follow Up Date: Sorts by date (oldest-newest/newest-oldest) 

Researcher Name: Sorts alphabetically 

Recovery ID: Sorts numerically (lowest-highest/highest-lowest) 

SLA: Sorts numerically 

   

Acceptance Criteria: 

Sort & Filter options needs to be available in the case listing page 

  

Given that user has access to ROC UTW Recoveries Case listing page 

When there is sort or filter the claim options are needed 

Then the user should have the provisions in Case Listing page 

 